  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1149 PM CDT Fri Jun 26 2026\n\nThe forecast remains benign through most of next week. The upper \nlevel ridge will remain the primary influence over our day to day \nweather through the next 7 days. By early next week the center of \nthe ridge axis shifts to the east of our area in response to a \nbroad upper level trough over the western CONUS. Western portions\nof Crockett County may be far enough west to see an isolated\nshower or thunderstorm develop Monday evening. Otherwise, we will\nmaintain a generally hot and dry forecast. We may be close to \nheat advisory criteria on Sunday across portions of the Big \nCountry but will hold off on issuing any products with this \npackage. For most of the area highs will climb into the upper 90s\nto near 103 degrees Saturday though Wednesday. The status quo \nwill continue through the latter part of of next week, with highs \non Thursday and Friday in the mid 90s to near 104 degrees.",
